[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=FileDir's window, the list you hear, the dialogs that all work one way, and where help is, each named and then shown by the reader; then the rules every key follows, so a key can be guessed before it is learned.
Setup=FileDir is open on a folder of your own, such as Documents.
Homework=Open a folder and name each thing as you reach it: the list, the line, the status line.

[step]

Say=One want: to move around FileDir without hunting. Everything in it follows a few rules, and this walk shows each one as the screen reader hears it.
Key=

[step]

Say=FileDir is one window, and its main view is a list box: one line for each file or folder in the folder you are in.
Key=Insert+Tab
Hear=Documents, list box, Budget dot xlsx, 1 of 42
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Marks on a line say its kind. A backslash after a name means a folder.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Letters backslash, 2 of 42
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter on a folder goes into it. Comma, or Shift plus Backspace, comes back up a level.
Key=Comma
Hear=Documents, list box
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The Apostrophe says the current item's name. Shift plus Apostrophe says the name of the folder it is in.
Key=Apostrophe
Hear=Budget dot xlsx
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Z, Say Status, reads the status line: the item's date and size, the sort order, and any filter.
Key=Alt+Z
Hear=Budget dot xlsx, 14 kilobytes, modified 3 October 2026, sorted by name
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Tagging marks the files a command will act on. The Semicolon tags the current item, and a greater-than sign before a name means it is tagged.
Key=Semicolon
Hear=Tagged
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The Slash untags it again. Control plus A tags everything, and Control plus Shift plus A untags everything.
Key=Slash
Hear=Untagged
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Several folders can be open at once, each in its own window. Control plus O opens a folder in a new window.
Key=Control+O
Hear=Open Folder dialog, Folder: edit combo
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Text boxes that ask for a folder complete the path as you type, and remember your recent answers: Up Arrow brings back the last one.
Key=Up Arrow
Hear=C colon backslash Users backslash Downloads
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Every dialog works the same way: a label and its control, Tab between them, Alt with the underlined letter to jump to one, Control plus Enter for OK, and Escape to cancel.
Key=Escape
Hear=Documents, list box
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F4 says the titles of all the open windows, and Control plus Tab moves between them.
Key=Shift+F4
Hear=2 windows: Documents, Downloads
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A zip archive opens like a folder: Enter goes in, and its files are listed like any others.
Key=

[step]

Say=Help is in four places, the same in every Homer program. F1 opens the guide, the whole program in one document.
Key=F1
Hear=FileDir Guide
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F1 opens the history of changes, and Alt plus F1 says the version and offers a newer one if there is one.
Key=Alt+F1
Hear=About FileDir dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes it. The Help menu, F10 then H, holds all of these, and Play Tutorials, which plays these walks.
Key=Escape
Hear=Documents, list box
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus H, Hotkey Summary, lists every key with its command and what it does, in a window you can search.
Key=Alt+Shift+H
Hear=Hotkey Summary
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Every key is named for a word in its command: Control plus J for Jump, Control plus O for Open, Shift plus C for Copy to Folder. A key never comes from the middle of a word.
Key=Escape
Hear=Documents, list box
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F1 is the Key Describer. While it is on, every key says what it does instead of doing it: the safe way to explore.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer on
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now Shift plus Z only says what it would do.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=Shift plus Z, Zip, add current or tagged files to zip archive
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F1 again turns the describer off.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer off
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Two settings are worth knowing now. Configuration Options, Alt plus Shift plus C, names your word processor, editor and player. Alt plus Shift plus R decides whether deleting sends to the Recycle Bin.
Key=Alt+Shift+R
Hear=Recycle on
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Messages are spoken as they happen, and shown on the status line, so one that is missed can be read again with the reader's own key for that line.
Key=

[step]

Say=A short review. I say a command; the reader says its key. Rename the current item.
Key=
Hear=F2, or Shift plus R

[step]

Say=Copy the tagged items to another folder.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus C

[step]

Say=Move them.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus M

[step]

Say=Zip them.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus Z

[step]

Say=Go to the parent folder.
Key=
Hear=Comma, or Shift plus Backspace

[step]

Say=Jump to an item by part of its name.
Key=
Hear=Control plus J

[step]

Say=Every one of these is in Hotkeys, in the Help menu, listed by key and by command.
Key=

